    turnFlow: 'Each player receives one piece from the bag (or deck), kept secret. Starting left of the dealer and going clockwise, each player may keep their piece (stand) or offer to swap with their left-hand neighbour. The neighbour must accept the swap unless they hold a matador (Knight, Bird, Cat, or Inn). Knight stops trading and the swap attemptor pays a token; Bird refuses with no penalty; Cat undoes all swaps so far; Inn forces the attemptor to swap with the next player instead. The dealer may swap with a piece drawn from the bag. When the swap round ends, everyone reveals; the player with the lowest piece pays one token to the pool. Fool (Jan Rit) is lowest; its holder must knock; both fool-holder and next-lowest pay. Last player with chips wins.',
